# What never enters an image.
#
# Patterns are anchored at the build context root unless they start with `**/`, so anything
# that can exist at more than one depth is written both ways round. Getting that wrong is
# silent: the file is simply copied.

# Secrets first, and by pattern rather than by name: an image is copied, pushed and inspected
# by more parties than a working tree is, and a credential baked into one layer is not removed
# by deleting the file in a later one.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
docker/env/*.env

# Local planning documents. Untracked, and not container material either.
ARCHITECTURE_PLAN.md
PROMISEPATCH_PRODUCT_SPEC.md

# History and tooling state.
.git
.github
.claude
.mcp.json

# Environments and caches: rebuilt inside the image, and a host virtualenv or a host
# `node_modules` is built for the wrong platform in any case.
.venv
venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.import_linter_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov

# Build output and test artefacts.
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report

# Editors and OS.
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
